From a4fafd1cf611cc1c77aad38c013c35a4f5e5ed35 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 04:45:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Pause really pauses in every take mode

Pause now closes each camera's file and resume starts the next piece, so the
paused stretch is never recorded; stop joins the pieces, checks the join and
only then removes them. Camcorder, data-only and main-camera takes all pause:
show data keeps nothing from a pause and a main-camera program is assembled on
take time with the pause removed. Replaces the suspend approach, which still
wrote the paused stretch once the encoder woke.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
